-- ind-a-tests-duties.l4: duties and powers of ss.5 to 17 whose only answer in the encoding is a regulative rule.
-- A duty that binds unconditionally, or a power whose preconditions hold, must be a live rule (not FULFILLED);
-- a power whose precondition fails must be FULFILLED (nothing arises).  This checks that the duty or power
-- exists and is gated as the source gates it; it does not check the modal (MUST against MAY).
-- Expected values decided before the encoding was opened (work/ind-a/expectations.md).

§ `ind-a helper`

GIVEN p IS A TYPE
      a IS A TYPE
      d IS A DEONTIC p a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a is fulfilled` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `Duties that bind`

-- S05-03: the Registrar must publish how to apply and the documents list.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 5(c) — the Registrar must publish how to apply and the documents to attach`)
-- S07-07: the Director of the Division must publish instructions for applying for an exemption.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 7(c) — the Director must publish the instructions for applying for an exemption`)
-- S11-01: the Registrar must keep a register.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 11(a) — the Registrar must keep a register of licensees`)
-- S10-21: after a revocation under (a), with the Council consulted, the Registrar must direct the waiting period.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 10(d) — the Registrar must direct the period before a new application may be made` (`Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)` WITH `the licence was revoked under section 10(a)` IS TRUE, `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE, `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE))
-- S17-14: (e) and (f).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s.17(e) — the Registrar must ensure that the trainings exist and are available`)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s.17(f) — the Registrar must publish the trainings on the Ministry website`)

§ `Powers gated by their preconditions`

-- S06-12: s.6(b) needs the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee's approval.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 6(b) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 6(b) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` FALSE)
-- S07-01, S07-02: s.7(a) needs a valid electricity licence of a listed kind.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 7(a) — the Director may exempt the applicant from the electricity chapter of the training` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 7(a) — the Director may exempt the applicant from the electricity chapter of the training` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE))
-- S07-04, S07-05: s.7(b) needs a valid height approval.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 7(b) — the Director may exempt the applicant from the working-at-height chapter of the training` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 7(b) — the Director may exempt the applicant from the working-at-height chapter of the training` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE))
-- S05-01, S05-02: s.5(b).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 5(b) — the Registrar may require information or a document` (`Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` WITH `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application` IS TRUE, `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application` IS TRUE))
#ASSERT `ind-a is fulfilled` (`s 5(b) — the Registrar may require information or a document` (`Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` WITH `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application` IS TRUE, `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application` IS FALSE))

§ `Second Schedule: "up to N hours" is a ceiling, not hours the applicant must reach (SCH2-A1c)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Second Schedule — the hours the applicant must complete under` (`training of up to` 350 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)
#ASSERT `Second Schedule — the ceiling on the hours of` (`training of up to` 350 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`) EQUALS 350
